'\" t
.TH OBJDUMP01 1 "October 2026" "mc6801-tools" "mc6801-tools Manual"
.SH NAME
objdump01, nm01, size01 \- display information about MC6801 executables
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B objdump01
.RB [ \-n | \-s ]
.RB [ \-o ]
.I file
\&...
.br
.B nm01
.RB [ \-o ]
.I file
\&...
.br
.B size01
.I file
\&...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B objdump01
displays the contents of a.out executables produced by
.BR ld01 (1).
.B make install
also installs it as
.B nm01
and
.BR size01 ,
which behave as if
.B \-n
or
.B \-s
had been given.
The mode is chosen from the first letter of the program name.
.PP
By default
.B objdump01
prints for each file:
.IP \(bu 2
the header: header length, CPU (m6801), flags, entry point
.RB ( a_entry ),
total memory size
.RB ( a_total )
and symbol table size;
.IP \(bu
the segment sizes;
.IP \(bu
the symbol table;
.IP \(bu
a hex and ASCII dump of the text and data segments.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-n
Print only the symbol table, like
.BR nm (1).
Each line gives the value, a type letter and the name.
.TP
.B \-s
Print only the text, data and bss sizes, in decimal, followed by the total
in decimal and hexadecimal, like
.BR size (1).
If several files are given, a total line is added.
.TP
.B \-o
In
.B \-n
mode, prefix each line with the file name instead of printing a
heading for each file.
.SH SYMBOL TYPES
.TS
l l.
\fBT\fP, \fBt\fP	text segment symbol (global, local)
\fBD\fP, \fBd\fP	data segment symbol (global, local)
\fBC\fP, \fBb\fP	bss or common symbol (global, local)
\fBa\fP	absolute symbol
\fBU\fP	undefined
\fB?\fP	other
.TE
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.B $ size01 main.aout
text	data	bss	dec	hex	filename
108	0	0	108	6c	main.aout
.sp
.B $ nm01 main.aout
0000434c t msg_one
00004351 T one
00004380 T __start
00004000 a SCREEN
\&...
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ld01 (1),
.BR objcopy01 (1),
.BR as01 (1)
.PP
The mc6801\-tools User\(aqs Manual
.RI ( mc6801\-tools\-manual.pdf ).
.SH BUGS
.B objdump01
cannot read object files made by
.BR as01 (1)
and reports \(lqBad magic number\(rq for them.
It still expects the original 8086 object format.
Use the
.B \-l
and
.B \-s
listing options of
.BR as01 (1)
to inspect assembled modules.
.PP
The text and data segments are shown as hex dumps, not disassembled.
.PP
Symbol names are cut to 8 characters.
.PP
Unknown options are silently ignored.
.SH HISTORY
Derived from
.B objdump86
in the dev86 package, by Greg Haerr and others.
